# Google Drive Integration - Environment Variables Template
# ============================================================
# 
# USAGE:
# 1. Copy this file to .env.staging and .env.production
# 2. Fill in the values for your environment
# 3. Source with: source .env.staging (for development/testing)
# 4. Or set in Supabase dashboard > Settings > Environment Variables
#
# NEVER commit actual credentials to git!
# Add *.local and .env.* to .gitignore

################################################################################
# STAGING ENVIRONMENT
################################################################################

# Supabase Connection (Staging)
STAGING_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-staging-project.supabase.co
STAGING_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-staging-anon-key-here
STAGING_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-staging-service-role-key-here

# Google OAuth (Staging)
# Obtain from: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application type)
# Add redirect URI: https://your-staging-project.supabase.co/functions/v1/google-oauth-callback
STAGING_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-staging-google-client-id-here
STAGING_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-staging-google-client-secret-here

# Edge Function Configuration (Staging)
STAGING_GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL=https://your-staging-project.supabase.co/functions/v1/google-oauth-callback

# Optional: Advanced Configuration
STAGING_GOOGLE_DRIVE_SEARCH_LIMIT=40
STAGING_GOOGLE_DRIVE_RESULT_LIMIT=5
STAGING_ENABLE_GOOGLE_LOGGING=true

################################################################################
# PRODUCTION ENVIRONMENT
################################################################################

# Supabase Connection (Production)
PROD_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-production-project.supabase.co
PROD_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-production-anon-key-here
PROD_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-production-service-role-key-here

# Google OAuth (Production)
# Obtain from: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application type)
# Add redirect URI: https://your-production-project.supabase.co/functions/v1/google-oauth-callback
PROD_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-production-google-client-id-here
PROD_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-production-google-client-secret-here

# Edge Function Configuration (Production)
PROD_GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL=https://your-production-project.supabase.co/functions/v1/google-oauth-callback

# Optional: Advanced Configuration
PROD_GOOGLE_DRIVE_SEARCH_LIMIT=40
PROD_GOOGLE_DRIVE_RESULT_LIMIT=5
PROD_ENABLE_GOOGLE_LOGGING=false

################################################################################
# DEVELOPMENT ENVIRONMENT (Local Testing)
################################################################################

# Supabase Connection (Local/Development)
DEV_SUPABASE_URL=http://localhost:54321
DEV_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
DEV_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# Google OAuth (Development)
# For local development, use public testing credentials or localhost redirect
DEV_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-dev-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
DEV_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-dev-client-secret

# Edge Function Configuration (Development)
DEV_GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL=http://localhost:5173/auth/callback

################################################################################
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
################################################################################

# 1. OBTAIN GOOGLE OAUTH CREDENTIALS
# ====================================
#
# Step 1: Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/
# Step 2: Create a new project or select existing one
# Step 3: Enable Google Drive API:
#   - Go to APIs & Services > Library
#   - Search for "Google Drive API"
#   - Click it and press "Enable"
# Step 4: Create OAuth 2.0 credentials:
#   - Go to APIs & Services > Credentials
#   - Click "Create Credentials" > "OAuth client ID"
#   - Choose "Web application"
#   - Add authorized JavaScript origins:
#     - For staging: https://your-staging-project.supabase.co
#     - For production: https://your-production-project.supabase.co
#     - For development: http://localhost:5173
#   - Add authorized redirect URIs:
#     - For staging: https://your-staging-project.supabase.co/functions/v1/google-oauth-callback
#     - For production: https://your-production-project.supabase.co/functions/v1/google-oauth-callback
#     - For development: http://localhost:5173/auth/callback
# Step 5: Copy Client ID and Client Secret below

# 2. SET UP SUPABASE PROJECT
# ===========================
#
# For Staging:
#   - Create new Supabase project (or use existing "staging" project)
#   - Go to Settings > General
#   - Copy Project URL and paste as STAGING_SUPABASE_URL
#   - Go to Settings > API
#   - Copy anon key and paste as STAGING_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#   - Copy service role key and paste as STAGING_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#
# For Production:
#   - Use existing production Supabase project
#   - Repeat above steps with PROD_* variables

# 3. CONFIGURE EDGE FUNCTION ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ==================================================
#
# In Supabase Dashboard:
#   1. Go to Edge Functions
#   2. For each function (google-oauth-start, google-oauth-callback, google-connector, vision-rag-query):
#      - Click function name
#      - Click "Settings"
#      - Add environment variables:
#        - GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
#        - GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
#        - GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL
#
# Or set via CLI:
#   supabase secrets set GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=... GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=... --project-id your-project-id

# 4. LOCAL DEVELOPMENT SETUP
# ===========================
#
# 1. Copy this file to .env.local
# 2. Fill in DEV_* variables with your local/staging values
# 3. Source it: source .env.local
# 4. Start local Supabase: supabase start
# 5. Run frontend: npm run dev (from frontend directory)

################################################################################
# SECURITY NOTES
################################################################################

# ⚠️  NEVER commit this file with actual credentials to git
# ⚠️  Add to .gitignore: .env.* *.local secrets/
# ⚠️  Client Secret should NEVER be in frontend code
# ⚠️  Only send Client Secret from backend/Edge Functions
# ⚠️  Use environment variable management (AWS Secrets Manager, Vault, etc.)
# ⚠️  Rotate credentials regularly
# ⚠️  Use separate credentials per environment (dev, staging, prod)
# ⚠️  Monitor Google Cloud Console for API usage and quota

################################################################################
# VERIFICATION CHECKLIST
################################################################################

# Before deploying, verify:
# [ ] Google Client ID is set and matches Google Cloud Console
# [ ] Google Client Secret is set and secure
# [ ] Supabase URLs are correct (no typos)
# [ ] Redirect URI is exactly as configured in Google Cloud Console
# [ ] Service role key is set (for backend operations)
# [ ] Environment variables are NOT in git repository
# [ ] Each environment has separate credentials
# [ ] Credentials have been rotated (if reusing old ones)

# Test with:
#   ./deploy-google-integration-staging.sh --validate-only

################################################################################
# TROUBLESHOOTING
################################################################################

# Issue: "Invalid client" error during OAuth
#   Solution: Check GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID matches Google Cloud Console
#
# Issue: "Redirect URI mismatch" error
#   Solution: Verify GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL exactly matches Google Console
#
# Issue: "Client secret not found" error
#   Solution: Set GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET in Supabase Edge Function settings
#
# Issue: "Invalid grant" error
#   Solution: User may not have Google Drive access, check with user's account
#
# Issue: Functions can't access environment variables
#   Solution: Verify variables are set in Supabase dashboard, not just locally

# For more help, see: QUICK_REFERENCE_GOOGLE_INTEGRATION.md
